course: dictionary
lesson: 5952
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-3
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, so check the words around it. The context tells you which meaning fits. «Wipe your feet on the mat before you come in» tells you a mat is something on the floor, near the door.
explain: Now read «Put your hot dish on a mat so the table does not get burnt.» This mat is not on the floor. It is a small flat piece under a hot dish, to protect the table. The clues are hot dish and table.
explain: In PE, a mat is thick and soft. «The gymnast landed safely on the thick, soft mat» tells you it is a gym mat, which protects you when you fall. Always ask: what is the mat for, and where is it?
fact: A mat is a small piece of material put on the floor, like a doormat or bath mat.
fact: A gym or yoga mat is a thick, soft piece of material for exercise.
fact: A placemat is a small flat piece put under a plate, glass or hot dish to protect the table.
fact: Matt, with two t's, is a different word. It means not shiny, so matt paint has no shine.
fact: To check your meaning, put it into the sentence in place of the hard word. If it still makes sense, you are probably right.
exercise: «Please wipe your feet on the mat before you come in.» Where is the mat? | Inside the fridge | *On the floor by the front door | On the top of a tall tree | On the ceiling above the bed
exercise: «The gymnast landed safely on the thick, soft mat.» What kind of mat is it? | A placemat | *A gym mat | A doormat | A bath mat
exercise: «Put the hot dish on a mat so the table does not get burnt.» What is the mat for? | To make the dish colder | To keep the dog warm | To make the table shine | *To protect the table from the heat
test: «Put your glass on the placemat.» What does placemat mean? | A kind of paper for drawing | A sports shirt | A big bed for sleeping | *A small flat piece under a glass or plate
test: Ben says «matt» paint is very shiny. What is true? | Matt means very shiny, so Ben is right | *Matt means not shiny, so Ben is wrong | Matt means a small piece for the floor | Matt means very loud
exam: Read: «Mats are useful in PE, because they soften a fall.» What does mat mean here? | *A thick, soft piece of material for exercise | A piece of material on the floor by the door | A small flat piece under a hot dish | A kind of shiny paint
